<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons for Arcane Mage DPS Phase 1 Pre-Raid</h3>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-weapons-for-arcane-mage-dps-phase-1-pre-raid">Main-Hand Weapons for Arcane Mage DPS Phase 1 Pre-Raid</h4>One handed weapons have worse stats than staves for arcane mage, mostly because they all have critical strike rating for some reason as a secondary except for the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69844/vitreous-beak-of-julak-doom">
<img alt="Vitreous Beak of Julak-Doom" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_knife_1h_cataclysm_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vitreous Beak of Julak-Doom</span></a> which isn't recommended due to how rare and expensive it'll be.<br/>
<br/>They're ordered in terms of relative performance assuming the best pre-raid offhand, but I'd recommend just grabbing the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62458/insidious-staff">
<img alt="Insidious Staff" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stave_2h_cataclysm_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Insidious Staff</span></a> reputation staff as a baseline weapon and then go from there.<br/>
<br/>The other three weapons are about the same as the crafted dagger, but require them actually dropping from heroic dungeons.<div class="quote-box" data-has-source="false" data-type="user">
<div class="quote-header"></div>
<div class="quote-body" data-markup-content-target="1">
